VERA20k @VERSION@ (early alpha)

VERA20k is a free, open-source reimplementation of Command & Conquer: Yuri's
Revenge. It contains no game files: you need your own copy of Yuri's Revenge
1.001, for example from The Ultimate Collection on Steam or the EA app.

GETTING STARTED
Either:
  - copy these files into your Yuri's Revenge folder (the one with gamemd.exe)
    and start vera20k there, or
  - keep them in a folder of your own, copy config.toml.example to config.toml
    and set ra2_dir to your game folder, with forward slashes, for example
    ra2_dir = "C:/Games/Yuri's Revenge"

VERA20k writes logs/, saves/ and replays/ in the folder you start it from; the
log is logs/ra2.log. If your game folder is under Program Files, which Windows
protects from writing, use the second option.

REQUIREMENTS
  A GPU with Vulkan, DirectX 12 or Metal.
  Windows: SmartScreen may warn about an unknown app; choose More info, then
    Run anyway.
  macOS: the program is not notarized by Apple yet, so macOS refuses to open
    it as downloaded. Open Terminal, type cd and a space, drag this folder
    onto the Terminal window and press Return. Then run these two lines; the
    first removes macOS's "downloaded from the internet" mark from this one
    program, and you only need it once:
      xattr -d com.apple.quarantine vera20k
      ./vera20k
  Linux: needs ALSA (libasound2) and a Vulkan driver.

This is early software: expect missing features and differences from the
original game. Report them at https://github.com/YuriPlanet/vera20k/issues

Official downloads come only from
https://github.com/YuriPlanet/vera20k/releases. To check that an archive was
built there, run: gh attestation verify <archive> --repo YuriPlanet/vera20k

